From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:14:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] canserial: Vary discovery slots between queries

Discovery slot selection was deterministic for a given UUID.  If two unassigned nodes mapped to the same slot, their same-identifier responses collided; every later query selected the same slot and repeated the collision, making both nodes permanently invisible to discovery.

Seed the UUID hash with a counter that advances for each accepted discovery query.  This gives every node a changing deterministic slot sequence without depending on a hardware random-number source.  A collision in one round therefore does not force the same pair of responses to collide on every retry.

Update the protocol documentation to state why slot selection changes between queries.

Signed-off-by: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>

diff --git a/docs/CANBUS_protocol.md b/docs/CANBUS_protocol.md
index 04f41852..534d3619 100644
--- a/docs/CANBUS_protocol.md
+++ b/docs/CANBUS_protocol.md
@@ -38,7 +38,8 @@ delay that response by an interval derived from their `canbus_uuid` so
 that multiple unassigned nodes do not normally transmit the response
 with the same CAN bus id at the same time. Response slots are separated
 by enough time to transmit the complete response at the configured CAN
-bus frequency.
+bus frequency, and the slot selection changes on later queries so that
+a collision in one discovery round does not persist indefinitely.
 
 The CMD_QUERY_UNASSIGNED message format is:
 `<1-byte message_id = 0x00>`
diff --git a/src/generic/canserial.c b/src/generic/canserial.c
index 9a60d1e0..c5c1977f 100644
--- a/src/generic/canserial.c
+++ b/src/generic/canserial.c
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@ static struct canbus_data {
     // Tx data
     struct task_wake tx_wake;
     struct timer query_timer;
+    uint32_t query_number;
     uint8_t transmit_pos, transmit_max, query_state;
 
     // Rx data
@@ -235,7 +236,16 @@ can_process_query_unassigned(struct canbus_msg *msg)
     uint32_t slot_count = CAN_QUERY_RESPONSE_WINDOW_US / slot_us;
     if (!slot_count)
         slot_count = 1;
-    uint32_t uuid_slot = CanData.uuid[0] | CanData.uuid[1] << 8;
+    /*
+     * A UUID-only slot is deterministic.  If two nodes happen to select the
+     * same slot, every later discovery query would reproduce the collision and
+     * neither node could ever be discovered.  Use the accepted-query count as
+     * a hash seed so each node follows a different deterministic slot sequence.
+     * This does not require a hardware random-number source, and a collision in
+     * one discovery round no longer forces the same collision on every retry.
+     */
+    uint32_t uuid_slot = fasthash64(CanData.uuid, sizeof(CanData.uuid),
+                                    CanData.query_number++);
     uint32_t delay = 100 + uuid_slot % slot_count * slot_us;
     CanData.query_state = CQS_WAITING;
     CanData.query_timer.waketime = timer_read_time() + timer_from_us(delay);
